{"title":"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems\">2012 AMC 12A #4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems\">2012 AMC 10A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a bag of marbles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the marbles are blue and the rest are red. If the number of red marbles is doubled and the number of blue marbles stays the same, what fraction of the marbles will be red?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5738925616c839d4f4fb65f07d173838053796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"367\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume that there are 5 total marbles in the bag. The actual number does not matter, since all we care about is the ratios, and the only operation performed on the marbles in the bag is doubling.\n</p><p>There are 3 blue marbles in the bag and 2 red marbles. If you double the amount of red marbles, there will still be 3 blue marbles but now there will be 4 red marbles. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042933304954135ca2ca571ea8b541ec9f56f043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us say that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> marbles in the bag. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad56bb341dfd47b5d6e60040d6d7b37e2652cd3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3x}{5x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> are blue, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4ff0a9dcd87fd72c98682c0c57563c255b9ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x}{5x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"21\" height=\"37\" /> are red. When the red marbles are doubled, we now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6738051db3f3f773bcdf378960b4553e302957a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2*2x}{5x+2x} = \\frac{4x}{7x} = \\frac{4}{7} \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"218\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> marbles in total. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> are blue, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue marbles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red marbles.\n</p><p>If the number of red marbles is doubled, then the number of red marbles becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, while the number of blue marbles remains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the new total number of marbles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0720aa8f7e4c3eefe3960ad92282609edafb5a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and the fraction of marbles that are red is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e418cb8fb0c830e7ad6eb1e2c03056fd51d8c45e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/b/d0b0e038c6bd8d904556544e7cb46c52f2d3c6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{4}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"26\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc73fea02e84d95c33ab71708c9398cd77b070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(Solution by Trashboycan)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9JCo1Qmsf6s\">https://youtu.be/9JCo1Qmsf6s</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SjMfmDWhWX0\">https://youtu.be/SjMfmDWhWX0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A\">2012 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"20